chnology Services University Marketing & Communications Physical Plant & Work Requests Institutional Effectiveness Procurement University Advancement & Alumni Affairs Lander Leadership Board of Trustees President's Office Executive Leadership Academic Affairs Office of Dean of Students The Lander Foundation Center for Faculty Excellence South Carolina Institute on the Prevention of Sexual Violence on College Campuses Faculty Senate Staff Senate Search... Search Search Search Staff Vacancies Lander Home About Offices & Departments Human Resources Employment Opportunities Current: Staff Vacancies Employment Opportunities Staff Vacancies Faculty Vacancies Our team is made up of talented and driven professionals who are committed to making a meaningful impact every day. From application to graduation, we work together to create an exceptional experience for our students—and we’re always looking for dedicated individuals to join us in that mission. If you're passionate about excellence, collaboration, and helping others succeed, we invite you to explore our current job openings and become part of the Lander family. View current Lander University vacancies here. Application Procedure Status of Closed Positions Directions FAQs Employment Application Policy for Staff Positions Please review the following information before applying for employment. To access the job portal, go to careers.sc.gov . A completed State application on NEO-GOV is required for consideration of employment. Resumes may be attached. Click here for more information about applying using NEO-GOV . If you require accommodation with our online application service, please call (864) 388-8310 or email jpartlow@lander.edu . Applications are only accepted for current job vacancies. The Office of Human Resources does not keep applications and/or resumés on file for future vacancies. Status of Closed Positions Position Department Date Status Human Resources Specialist Human Resources 01/02/2026 Filled Front Desk Operations Assistant Admissions 01/02/2026 Filled Assistant Director of Content Strategy Marketing & Communications 12/01/2025 Filled Front Desk Operations Assistant Housing & Residence Life 01/09/2026 Filled IT Technician III ITS 01/09/2026 Filled Admissions Counselor Admissions 01/09/2026 Filled Assistant Men's Baseball Coach Athletics 02/02/2026 Filled Coordinator Of Fraternity And Sorority Life Campus Engagement 02/02/2026 Filled Head Men's Soccer Coach Athletics 02/02/2026 Filled Front Desk Operations Assistant Housing & Res Life 03/02/2026 Filled Videographer/ Photographer Marketing & Communication 03/16/2026 Filled Administrative Assitsant Athletics 03/16/2026 Filled Student Support Services Director Student Experience & Quality Assurance 03/16/2026 Filled Budget Manager Finance & Administration 03/16/2026 Filled Director of Sponsored Projects Finance & Administration 03/18/2026 Closed/ Not Filled Dean of Students Dean of Students 03/19/2026 Filled IT Consultant ITS 05/01/2026 Filled Plumber Physical Plant 05/01/2026 Filled Admissions Counselor Admissions 04/10/2026 Filled Coordinator of Course Articulation and Transfer Registrar 04/24/2026 Filled Executive Assistant Advancement 04/29/2026 Filled Director of University Web Content & Experience Marketing & Communications 05/01/2026 Filled Area Coordinator Housing & Residential Life 08/03/2026 Filled Assignments Coordinator Housing & Res Life 06/16/2026 Filled Senior Director of Revenue & Accounting Finance and Administration 05/10/2026 Closed/Not Filled Payroll Manager Finance & Administration 06/16/2026 Filled Communications Specialist (Dispatcher) University Police 06/16/2026 Filled Administrative Assistant (Arts & Humanities) Academic Affairs 06/01/2026 Filled Administrative Assistant (COE) College of Education 06/10/2026 Filled Academic Counselor Dean of Students 06/10/2026 Reviewing Applications Assistant Director of Paid Media & Marketing MarComm 06/16/2026 Filled Associate Head Wrestling Coach Athletics 06/10/2026 Filled Administrative Specialist (Arts & Humanities) Academic Affairs 06/16/2026 Filled Assistant Men's Soccer Coach Athletics 08/03/2026 Filled Benefits Counselor Human Resources 08/03/2026 Filled Assistant Director of Advancement Operations University Advancement 08/17/2026 Filled Assistant Director of Paid Media & Marketing Marketing & Communications 08/03/2026 Filled Assistant Men's Lacrosse Coach Athletice 08/03/2026 Filled Associate Vice President for Campaign Operations and Major Gifts University Advancement 08/03/2026 Filled Employee Relations Manager Human Resources 08/03/2026 Reviewing Applications Assistant Athletics Trainer Athletics 08/17/2026 Filled Student Records Coordinator Office of the Registrar 08/17/2026 Reviewing Applications Maintenance Manager Physical Plant 08/17/2026 Filled Coordinator Of Community Belonging Dean of Students 08/07/2026 Reviewing Applications Social Media Coordinator MARCOMM 08/05/2026 Reviewing Applications Director of Communications MARCOMM 08/05/2026 Reviewing Applications Directions We are located at 511 Willson Street, Greenwood. From the main Lander entrance on Calhoun Avenue: Turn onto Crews Street. (Located between the two fountains.) Go straight thru the first four way stop. At the second four way stop take a left onto Willson Street. Go approximately 0.3 miles and our office will be on your left. Please note: Parking is limited in our driveway, if you are coming in to fill out an application or meeting with a staff member we request that you park in the lot behind our office. To get to the lot: drive past the house and turn left onto Felder Street. Take an immediate left and keep left to get to the parking lot straight ahead. For handicap visitors: Please park in the Human Resources drive way and for special assistance call (864) 388-8310. >> Printable Campus Map (PDF) FAQs Will I get a phone call/letter when the position I applied for is filled? Applicants who select the email notification option on NEO-GOV will receive an email once the position applied for is filled. What are types of insurance is available to permanent positions? Health/dental/optional life/dependent life spouse/dependent life child/vision/long term disability and AFLAC are offered to permanent employees based on eligibility. How do I apply for a job in the Dining Hall? Lander contracts with Aramark for dining services. You may visit Dining Hall Employment for Aramark employment opportunities. Do you keep applications/resumes on file? We do not keep resumes or applications on file. To be considered for a position, you must submit an application online during the opening and closing dates. What are the methods of advertising for vacant positions? Vacant positions are advertised on careers.sc.gov . What student worker positions are available? All student work study positions must go through the Financial Aid Office . The Office of Human Resources occasionally has work study positions available in our office, but they are listed with Financial Aid when available. Can I fax or email my application? No, applications are only accepted online using careers.sc.gov . What if I don't have a computer at home? You can visit your local library or there is a computer kiosk in The Office of Human Resources that is available during our business hours. How long does a temporary position last? Typically, a temporary position may not exceed 12 months without a break. How will I know if I am selected for an interview? The hiring supervisor contacts selected candidates by phone or email to schedule an interview time. How does the interview process work? Once a job closes, the hiring supervisor/hiring committee receives the applications for review. They determine who is awarded an interview. The hiring supervisor will then contact those applicants to set up interview times. Depending on the position, a test, individual, or panel interview may be conducted. How will I know if I am selected for a job? After the hiring supervisor has selected a candidate, Human Resources completes a background check, then the Classification and Compensation Manager approves the compensation rate. Then the supervisor will contact the candidate to make an offer. Can I speak with the hiring supervisor of the position I applied for? If you are chosen for an interview, you will be contacted by the hiring supervisor. Due to the number of applications received, phone calls are discouraged. About the University Human Resources Employment Opportunities Staff Vacancies Faculty Vacancies Benefits Forms & Resources Faculty Senate Staff Senate Affordable Care Act Americans with Disabilities Act Employee of the Month Fair Labor Standards Act Holiday Schedule Inclement Weather Lander University EPMS System Volunteers Worker's Compensation 320 Stanley Ave, Greenwood, SC 29649 1-888-4LANDER | 864-388-8000 Questions? Contact Us! Lander University Instagram Lander University Facebook Lander University YouTube Lander University Linkedin Lander University X Â© Lander University. Privacy Policy . Clery Report Consumer Information Statement of Non-Discrimination Tucker Hipps Transparency Act Title IX Job Opportunities Report Fraud"
    },
